# pmi-workers supercronic crontab.
#
# Each line: <min> <hour> <dom> <month> <dow> <command>
#
# CORR-4.6 (cron → worker): schedule lines ENQUEUE onto the Postgres job queue
# (`core_jobs`); the long-lived `pmi-worker` compose service claims + executes
# (retry / heartbeat / dedupe live there). `pmi-workers enqueue` dedupes by
# job name+args, so a beat landing while the previous tick is still
# queued/running is a no-op instead of stacking — which also retires the old
# trailing-`&` pattern (enqueue is a sub-second INSERT).
#
# One-shot manual in-process execution still works: `run-job <name>`.
#
# FOUR LANES (one claim-loop container each — see docker-compose.yml):
#   default  → pmi-worker           on-demand `score` + the WS reeval-market fan-out
#   snapshot → pmi-worker-snapshot  the */10 page snapshots below. On the default
#                                   lane they queued 20-80 min behind ~700
#                                   reeval-market/score jobs an hour, so every board
#                                   flagged DELAYED while its scores were fresh
#                                   (2026-10-20).
#   batch    → pmi-worker-batch     hourly / reeval-drifted / tag-* whole-registry passes
#   long     → pmi-worker-long      daily (embed + full re-score, ~2.5 h), tag-games,
#                                   workflow — serialised on their own so they no
#                                   longer park `hourly` for a morning.
# History: with ONE lane and worker_concurrency=2 the two long passes held both
# slots and every snapshot waited behind them (07-07); the batch split fixed
# that, and the WS fan-out then crowded the snapshots out of `default` (10-20).
#
# The lane is NOT chosen here — each job declares it via `@register(...,
# queue="batch")` and `enqueue` reads that. Keeping the choice at the call site
# meant one producer forgetting the flag re-created the starvation; the rule
# ("batch for anything that walks every index, default for anything a page
# waits on") now lives with the job. `--queue` still overrides per-line.

# Hourly: re-score every current PMI definition.
0 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue hourly

# Every 30 min (batch lane): (re)classify election markets into
# core_market_race_tag — the membership source the us-{senate,house,governor} +
# maga-{senate,house,governor} indexes select from (WHERE office/cycle, no
# keyword-pool cap). Runs the keyword path's own classification, so newly
# ingested race legs get tagged and picked up by the next score. Tag freshness
# isn't latency-critical (new race markets are rare), and it's a full scan, so it
# sits in the batch lane and offset from the :00 score / :10 board snapshots.
15,45 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue tag-races

# Every 5 min: rebuild core_market_priority — the P0 (in-use) / P1 (new listing)
# id lists the ingest pollers read when INGEST_PRIORITY_ENABLED=true. PK lookups
# only (never a core_markets scan); harmless while the flag is off, and the
# table doubles as the measurement for docs/reports/priority_ingestion_blueprint.md.
# --priority 10: a seconds-long job that must not queue behind board snapshots
# (2026-10-13 it waited 20–85 min in the default lane at the default 100).
*/5 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue refresh-market-priority --priority 10

# Every 10 min: pre-compute MAGA, Senate, House, Governor boards into ts_page_cache.
# maga-snapshot must run before governor-board-snapshot (governor reads maga cache).
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue maga-snapshot
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue senate-board-snapshot
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue house-board-snapshot
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue governor-board-snapshot
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue gdp-board-snapshot

# Every 10 min: pre-compute the war index (country→region→world) into ts_page_cache.
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue war-snapshot

# Every 10 min: pre-compute the Climate & Weather hub + boards into ts_page_cache.
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue climate-snapshot

# Every 10 min: pre-compute the markets boards into ts_page_cache (against the
# main `pmi` DB). Same cadence as the other boards; live-computing it on the hot
# path over ~2M markets times out, so the route serves this snapshot.
# One line per markets-board vertical — the job takes the index_id, and an index
# with no line here falls back to live compute on every single request (which is
# what made /micah/sp500 a ~4s page while /micah/markets served in ~0.7s).
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue markets-board-snapshot
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue markets-board-snapshot --args '{"index_id": "sp500-bull-bear-index"}'

# Every 10 min: pre-compute the esports match board + per-match detail into
# ts_page_cache. esports was the one vertical that live-computed per request
# (re-fold + trend scans, ~2.5s); it now serves from this snapshot like the rest.
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue esports-snapshot

# Every 10 min: pre-compute the Sports vertical boards (MLB / NFL) into
# ts_page_cache, one cache row per sport. Serves /sports/{sport} like the rest.
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue sports-snapshot

# Every 10 min: pre-compute the LoL Worlds tournament board (structure + live odds
# + resolved results) into ts_page_cache. Serves /worlds like the rest; its own
# cache row per tournament id, separate from esports.
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue worlds-snapshot

# Every 10 min: pre-compute the homepage's landing data (per-index cards + movers +
# stats) into ts_page_cache so "/" serves from one cached read instead of its
# ~12-endpoint fan-out on every visit. Triggers pmi-web's /api/home-data (which
# owns the assembly) and stores the JSON.
*/10 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue home-snapshot

# Every 15 min (batch lane): deterministically tag Kalshi NFL games from their
# tickers (game winner + spread) — free, no LLM. Kalshi titles name only one team
# so the LLM tagger (tag-games) can't pair them; the ticker has the matchup + date.
# Frequent + cheap so new slates show without waiting on an LLM pass.
*/15 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue tag-sports-kalshi

# Every 15 min (batch lane): deterministically tag Gemini NFL/MLB games from their
# instrumentSymbol (sport + teams + date) — free, no LLM. Gemini titles are
# city-only so the LLM mis-labels sport AND teams; the symbol has both. Upserts
# every run so it also heals the LLM's old mis-tags.
*/15 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue tag-gemini

# Every 15 min (batch lane): correct Polymarket MLB game tags from raw.slug
# (mlb-mil-lad-2026-10-15) — the LLM reads both teams off the title but guesses the
# date wrong, so games never fold with the Kalshi game. Deterministic, free; runs
# after tag-games so freshly-tagged games get their real date next tick.
*/15 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue tag-sports-polymarket

# Hourly (batch lane): LLM-tag sports markets across the title-names-both-teams
# venues (polymarket/manifold/metaculus). Incremental + cached (only untagged-at-
# current-version markets are sent), so steady-state is cheap. Gemini is NOT here
# (deterministic tag-gemini owns it).
30 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue tag-games

# Hourly: pre-compute the landing page's "Today's top movers" (24h Δ across the
# four landing indexes' component markets) into ts_page_cache. Hourly is plenty
# for a homepage list and keeps the per-market price-diff query off the hot path.
0 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue movers-snapshot

# Hourly: choose the landing page's cross-venue example (the one question two
# exchanges price differently). Only the CHOICE is cached — /landing/venue-spread
# re-reads the two markets' prices per request — so the pair search's O(n^2)
# cosine join stays off the hot path without the card ever quoting a stale price.
20 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue venue-spread-snapshot

# Tier 3 (CORR-5.2): every 15 min, re-score only the indexes whose component
# prices drifted >= PMI_DRIFT_THRESHOLD_PCT points since that index was last
# scored. Cheap no-op when nothing drifted; keeps scores fresher than the
# hourly full pass. The baseline is the score's own as_of, so acting on a drift
# clears it — measuring against a fixed window instead kept one 10-point move
# "drifted" for 24h and re-scored the whole registry on every beat.
*/15 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue reeval-drifted

# Daily 00:10 UTC: the deterministic war daily note (D6) — world + per-region
# paragraphs and contract citations, templated from the enriched war:{cycle}
# snapshot (no LLM). Once a day on purpose: it reads as a dated editorial
# note, not a ticker. Batch lane; pure dict work.
10 0 * * * pmi-workers enqueue war-summary

# Daily 06:00 UTC: compute the Insights issue (chamber-spread lead, cross-venue
# gap pairs, settling-this-week, every-reading) and freeze it under
# insight:issue:{iso_week}. Batch lane — the gap-pairs self-join is the
# venue-spread cost; daily suits a weekly editorial product.
0 6 * * * pmi-workers enqueue insights-snapshot

# Daily 10:00 UTC: heavier maintenance (placeholder — currently same as hourly).
0 10 * * * pmi-workers enqueue daily

# Weekly (Monday 13:00 UTC): email the weekly-report subscribers the index
# digest. No-op (logged) when PMI_SMTP_HOST is unset or the list is empty.
0 13 * * 1 pmi-workers enqueue weekly-report

# Hourly: announce newly-launched indexes to the "new-index" subscribers
# (hero "Get our updates" form). Cheap no-op when nothing new — detection is
# "current defs with no core_index_announcements row".
15 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue notify-new-indexes

# Daily 11:00 UTC: prune ts_page_cache — latest-only keys keep newest 24 rows;
# trend keys (war:{cycle} / maga:{cycle}) thin to last-per-day beyond 90 days.
0 11 * * * pmi-workers enqueue page-cache-retention

# --- OpenAI Batch API (CORR-5.3, half-price nightly recompute) --------------
# Only meaningful when factors are bound to gpt-*/openai/* models AND
# OPENAI_API_KEY is set; with an all-ollama registry both jobs no-op cleanly.
0 2 * * * pmi-workers enqueue llm-batch-submit
*/30 * * * * pmi-workers enqueue llm-batch-poll
